 "intro": "Words for «maybe»: the expression and your degree of certainty influence the mood.",
 "palabras": [
  {
   "palabra": "quizá",
   "significado": "perhaps",
   "pron": "ki-THA",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is also written «quizás». It takes indicative or subjunctive, depending on your certainty.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "tal vez",
   "significado": "perhaps",
   "pron": "tal beth",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is two words. It works like «quizá»: «tal vez venga» or «tal vez viene».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "puede que",
   "significado": "it may be that",
   "pron": "PWE-de ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Always with the subjunctive: «puede que nieve». «Puede» does not change here.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "es probable que",
   "significado": "it is likely that",
   "pron": "es pro-BA-ble ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It asks for the subjunctive: «es probable que llueva». «Probable» is the opposite of «improbable».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "a lo mejor",
   "significado": "maybe",
   "pron": "a lo me-HOR",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Very common in speech. Unlike «quizá», it almost always takes the indicative: «a lo mejor viene».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "igual",
   "significado": "maybe (colloquial)",
   "pron": "i-GWAL",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "In Spain you hear it a lot: «igual llueve». It takes the indicative. It is very informal.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "seguro que",
   "significado": "I'm sure that",
   "pron": "se-GU-ro ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "Almost total certainty: indicative. «Seguro que vienes» is almost a statement.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "supongo que",
   "significado": "I suppose that",
   "pron": "su-PON-go ke",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It takes the indicative: «supongo que tienes frío». It is less certain than «sé que».",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "no sé si",
   "significado": "I don't know whether",
   "pron": "no SE si",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "set expression",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "«Si» without an accent means «whether». With an accent, «sí», it is «yes». It takes the indicative.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
   "palabra": "probablemente",
   "significado": "probably",
   "pron": "pro-ba-ble-MEN-te",
   "ipa": "",
   "cat": "adverb",
   "genero": "",
   "plural": "",
   "definida": "",
   "consejo": "It is formed from «probable» + «-mente». It allows indicative or subjunctive.",
   "nota": "",
   "oculta": false
  },
  {
